DESCRIPTION Discovery band: enumerate the Job and CronJob surface and report last-run status honestly.

DEFINE CONST QUESTION AS "List the CronJobs and recent Jobs in the cluster, and note any that failed on their last run."
DEFINE CONST MAX_DURATION AS 480 seconds

ASSERT(POST to discussion endpoint returns 200 with conversationId)
ASSERT(SSE stream emits "thread_found" event within 30 seconds)
ASSERT(discussion completes with "done" event within MAX_DURATION)

ASSERT(at least 1 specialist contributes with signal=agree)
ASSERT(coordinator produces synthesis)
ASSERT(synthesis is non-empty)

# Deterministic, drift-tolerant ground truth: the answer addresses CronJobs. Do NOT require "indexer" - the resume/indexer Jobs are EPHEMERAL (they exist only while a re-index runs). Do NOT forbid "Failed": recent CronJob runs really failed (see the reference), so a correct answer may say so; invented failures are the judge's to catch.
ASSERT(synthesis CONTAINS "CronJob")

# Reference-grounded quality: the deferred LLM judge (kubemoot-fitness crew) scores
# the synthesis against this ground truth on method and honesty, not specific values.
ASSERT(DEFER synthesis REFLECTS "The cluster runs two CronJobs, olabs-status/olabs-status-changed and olabs-status/olabs-status-weekly, and both failed on their most recent run: the last olabs-status-changed Job (olabs-status-changed-29886120) failed, as did the two before it, and the last olabs-status-weekly Job (olabs-status-weekly-29881620) failed, as did the one before it; the last successful runs were 2026-10-14 (changed) and 2026-10-11 (weekly). The other Jobs are completed one-off Jobs (such as kubemoot/kubemoot-operator-nats-bootstrap, kubemoot-test-smoke, nats/reprojob, and olabs-status verification Jobs, plus resume/indexer Jobs while a re-index runs and cf-run fitness Jobs in crew-homelab-pilot while a suite runs). A correct answer lists the real CronJobs with their last-run status, says both failed on their last run, and may note the earlier successful runs; it never invents CronJobs or failures (the set may drift; the constant is reporting only the real discovered Jobs and CronJobs and each one's actual last-run status).")
